Z||000000||Loki||02-20-2001||09:11 PM||||If an engine rebuild has a higer compression ratio? My new 86SE has a rebuild but unknown as to what went in..Runs awsome and very strong (spins em in 1st on an automatic) Just wondering if there was an easy way to tell if CR was bumped up at all?????/<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-20-2001||10:28 PM||||Do a compression check.  The guages are fairly inexpensive.  I take it that this is a V6.  I know that about stock for the L4 is supposed to be above 100 psi.  I believe the stock CR between the two arent that different, but I could be wrong.  Anyway, go and get that compression checker, and post your readings here.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
